    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1102">

                <pb facs="1141" n="1131" xml:id="pg1131"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.801/8–2749: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >McConaughy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-27T14:00:00+08:00">August 27, 1949—2
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 27—4:20 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3498. A. P. Pattison, local agents Isbrandtsen Co., informed ConGen they plan
                    bring SS <hi rendition="#italic">Flying Independent</hi> into Shanghai about
                    September 9. Vessel will be en route Hong Kong to Taku Bar and is expected load
                    cargo Hong Kong for Shanghai, Shanghai for Tientsin and Shanghai for USA via
                    Suez. Pattison states owners have agreed to call. In view Chinese naval vessel
                    having prevented British SS <hi rendition="#italic">Edith Moller</hi> from
                    entering Shanghai August 23 (refContel 3482, August 26<anchor n="65"
                        xml:id="d1102-f1"/>), it seems possible <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Independent</hi> may also be detained.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Nanking 1849, Hong Kong 212.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">McConaughy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
